# Chat Session Report - Admin Panel Bootstrap Columns

### Session Summary
- **Date:** November 2025
- **Version:** 0.9.17 → 0.9.18 (Patch Increment)
- **Work Type:** UI Layout Refinement – Admin Character Table

### What We Accomplished

#### 1. Rebuilt Table Columns Around Bootstrap
- **Explicit Columns** – Restored dedicated `Name`, `NPC`, `Clan`, and `Actions` headings so character data and controls stay visible at tablet widths (≈768 px)
- **Bootstrap Utilities** – Swapped custom flex/padding rules for Bootstrap’s utility classes to control alignment, spacing, and responsive behavior

#### 2. Guaranteed Action Button Visibility
- **Single Actions Column** – Consolidated view/edit/delete buttons into one column rendered as a `btn-group btn-group-sm`
- **Centered Header/Content** – Forced centered alignment and a fixed column width so header text and controls line up at every breakpoint

#### 3. Removed Unused Status Noise
- **Badge Helper Update** – Suppressed `draft` and `finalized` badges from `render_status_badge()` so empty UI fragments don’t render
- **Column Cleanup** – Dropped the unused status column entirely to reclaim horizontal space for character names

### Technical Implementation Details

#### `admin/admin_panel.php`
- Replaced the table header/row structure with Bootstrap-aligned columns (`text-start`, `text-center`, `btn-group`)
- Adjusted status badge helper to return nothing for irrelevant states and fall back gracefully for unknown statuses
- Narrowed the `Actions` column with inline width to keep controls centered and on-screen at 768 px

#### `js/admin_panel.js`
- Updated pagination button creation to emit Bootstrap button classes for consistent styling with the new table layout

### Files Modified
- `admin/admin_panel.php`
- `js/admin_panel.js`
- `VERSION.md`

### Impact Summary
- **Usability:** Operators can see names, NPC markers, clans, and action buttons without horizontal scrolling on tablets
- **Consistency:** Buttons now inherit Bootstrap styling, matching the rest of the admin UI refactor
- **Signal-to-Noise:** Removed unused status indicators, keeping the table focused on actionable data

